  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The requested bias, RMSE, correlation and model ranking against WOA23 must be computed on one common mask/grid covering the cells all compared fields share, and the ranking only on the cells all models cover.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all three models and WOA23 on the WOA23 1° grid, build one mask with `build_comparison_mask` and apply `.where(mask)` to every field before bias, RMSE and correlation; the default `ocean_only=True` is right here because WOA23 is the reference.",
        "Report `compute_difference_metrics`' `mean_data`/`mean_reference` over that shared sample; each model's own-grid global mean is a different quantity and their difference is not the bias on the shared cells — say so, and give the mask's cell counts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "The question asks both for native-grid global means and for comparisons/maps on WOA23's 1-degree grid, so calculations should be native for means while regridding is used only for the comparison maps and pattern statistics.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute each global mean on the model's own grid with its own `areacello`; regrid only for the maps, the RMSE and the pattern correlation on the common mask, using 'conservative' (going to a coarser grid) and stating the method since a regridded RMSE/correlation depends on it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The requested global SST means over ocean grids must be area-weighted surface means using all ocean grid points, not unweighted cell averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Global mean SST is area-weighted over the top level: Σ `tos`·`areacello` / Σ `areacello` over valid ocean cells, with the weights masked to those same cells; a plain `mean()` over (y, x) is wrong.",
        "`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'` for the spatial pattern correlation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are on native gn grids but GFDL-ESM4 is gr, already conservatively regridded, which affects masks, conservation and how \"native grid\" means are stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 `tos` is `gr`, already remapped to a 180×360 1° grid ('conserve_order1'), so its \"native\" mean and mask are the regridded ones; CESM2 (gx1v7, 100 km) and MPI-ESM1-2-LR (250 km) are `gn`.",
        "Resolution differs about 2.5× between CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR, so features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "tos is the top-cell bulk potential temperature, not a skin temperature and includes water under sea ice, so comparison with WOA23 0 m SST must note the top-cell versus 0 m mismatch.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`tos` is the bulk temperature of the top model cell, including under sea ice, so a global mean carries near-freezing polar values; top cells differ (CESM2 0–10 m, GFDL-ESM4 0–2 m, MPI-ESM1-2-LR 0–12 m), so \"SST\" is not the same layer across the models."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20 and must be CF-masked before any mean or bias calculation, or the sums and means will be corrupted.",
      "status": "summary_fallback",
      "fallback": "the notes failed the check",
      "violations": [
        "`um` is not in the selected fragments or the question"
      ],
      "rejected_notes": [
        "Land is 1e20, decoded to NaN by xarray; use NaN-aware reductions with weights masked to the same cells — a hand-rolled `(data*weights).sum()/weights.sum()` returns 0.0 at all-land columns instead of NaN.",
        "A value near 1e20 or 9.97e36 in any output is an unmasked fill value, not a result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "areacello is the tracer-cell horizontal area needed as the weight for each model's native-grid surface mean, so it constrains the global-mean calculation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Weight each mean by the model's own `areacello` (tracer-cell area, zero or missing over land); on a curvilinear grid it is the only correct area weight.",
        "Total ocean area differs between models by about a per cent because each resolves the coastline differently — state the area each mean was taken over rather than rescaling one model to another."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245.md",
      "sha256": "be5515ae7b8c8826c4e329bddcd5cbadc8e3e000292b7f6e83e1537af36a990c",
      "reason": "The historical runs are coupled simulations with free internal variability whose years are not synchronized with observed years, so the model-WOA23 comparison is a climatological bias assessment rather than a year-by-year validation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "These are coupled, single-member historical runs with their own internal variability: a 1971–2000 climatology is a legitimate statistic, but no match of individual years or event timing with WOA23 should be expected."
      ]
    }
